<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Funj Sultanate of Sennar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sennar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Funj Sultanate of Sennar was a Muslim state on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-nile">Blue Nile</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, founded in the early sixteenth century. It was a neighbour and rival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a>, and the two contested <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kordofan">Kordofan</a>, before Sennar was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 1821.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/funj-sultanate-of-sennar.jpg" alt="Funj Sultanate of Sennar" width="320" height="365" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LeGabrie · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Funj_Sultanate_1700.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
